# Frontend Constitution — <%= projectName %>

<!-- arbiter-managed: frontend-governance (#1124) -->

**Framework:** <%= _fw %>
**Status:** RATIFIED
**Scope:** FE001–FE006

---

## 1. Definitions

**Adapter / API layer**
Infrastructure boundary implementing all I/O operations (HTTP, storage, external APIs).
No business logic lives here.

**Domain layer**
Pure business logic with zero framework coupling (no UI framework, no browser APIs, no state libraries).

**Application layer**
Glue connecting domain logic to UI via composables / hooks / services.

**State store**
Restricted to synchronous, client-only state. No async actions, no API caching.

---

## 2. Non-Negotiables (MUST)

- All HTTP calls to the backend API MUST occur within the adapter/API layer.
- The domain layer MUST contain pure business logic — no UI framework, state library, or browser API imports.
- Server state MUST be managed via a data-fetching library with stale-while-revalidate strategy.
- Every API response MUST be validated by a schema validator (<%= _vl %>) at the system boundary.
- All errors MUST be normalized to a standard `AppError` shape and routed via a centralized notification bus.
- UI components MUST use semantic design tokens (`--bg-*`, `--text-*`, etc.), NOT raw palette colors.

---

## 3. Pillar Rules (FE001–FE006)

### FE001 — Governed ACL (Anti-Corruption Layer)

**MUST:**
- All I/O and external mutations MUST occur within the adapter/API layer.
- Access to external systems MUST be via port interfaces or data-fetching hooks.
- Linting MUST restrict `fetch`/HTTP client imports to the API layer only.

**FORBIDDEN:**
- Direct `fetch`, `axios`, or equivalent HTTP calls in UI components, composables/hooks, or state stores.
- Cross-module HTTP calls outside the API layer.

**Enforcement:**
- ESLint `no-restricted-imports`: forbid HTTP clients outside the adapter layer.
- CI grep check: `rg "fetch\(|axios\." src/*/ui` MUST be empty.

---

### FE002 — Headless Domain Logic

**MUST:**
- The domain layer MUST contain pure business logic with zero framework coupling.
- Domain modules MUST import only pure language constructs, validation schemas, date utilities, and standard `Error` classes.

**FORBIDDEN:**
- Importing the UI framework (<%= _fw %>) in the domain layer.
- Importing state management libraries in the domain layer.
- Accessing browser APIs (`window`, `document`, `localStorage`, `matchMedia`) in the domain layer.

**Enforcement:**
- CI grep check: `rg "localStorage|matchMedia|document\.|window\." src/*/domain` MUST be empty.
- Architectural boundary tests enforce domain purity.

---

### FE003 — Application Layer & State Management

**MUST:**
- Server state MUST be managed via a data-fetching library with stale-while-revalidate strategy.
- <%= _sm %> MUST be restricted to synchronous, client-only state (no async actions, no API caching).
- Query keys MUST be co-located with their API functions.

**FORBIDDEN:**
- Async actions in <%= _sm %>.
- Business logic in store getters.
- Manually caching API responses in a client store.

**Enforcement:**
- Code review: verify no async/await in <%= _sm %> actions.

---

### FE004 — Centralized Error Handling

**MUST:**
- All exceptions MUST be normalized to a standard `AppError` schema.
- Errors MUST be routed via a centralized feedback/notification bus.
- A global error interceptor MUST convert 4xx/5xx responses to `AppError` objects.
- UI components MUST consume `AppError` to display user-friendly messages.

**FORBIDDEN:**
- Swallowing errors without reporting.
- Ad-hoc alerts or component-level `try/catch` blocks that suppress errors.
- `console.error` as the primary error handling mechanism in production code.

**Enforcement:**
- Code review: verify all API errors route through the global interceptor.

---

### FE005 — Async UX Policy

**MUST:**
- User intent MUST be acknowledged immediately via visual feedback.
- A loading/skeleton state MUST appear for first loads (no cached data available).
- A background-refresh indicator MUST appear for stale-while-revalidate refreshes.
- Skeleton components MUST have fixed heights matching real content dimensions (anti-layout-shift).
- Interactive elements MUST enter a disabled/loading state during in-flight operations.

**FORBIDDEN:**
- Frozen UI (blocking the main thread).
- Interactive elements lacking a loading state during operations.
- Silent failures (errors must surface via the notification bus).
- Manual `isLoading` refs duplicating what the data-fetching library already provides.

**Enforcement:**
- Code review: verify loading-state semantics (first load vs. background refetch).
- Design QA: verify skeleton heights match loaded content.

---

### FE006 — Design Tokens & Multi-Theme

**MUST:**
- UI components MUST use semantic design tokens (`--bg-*`, `--text-*`, etc.) exclusively.
- Foundation/primitive tokens are abstract values and MUST NOT be referenced directly by components.
- Theme switching MUST be controlled via a `data-theme` attribute on `<html>`.
- The app MUST support at minimum `light`, `dark`, and `system` (default) themes.
- FOUC prevention MUST be implemented via an inline script applied BEFORE CSS loads.

**FORBIDDEN:**
- Raw palette color classes (`bg-white`, `text-gray-500`, etc.) in production UI files.
- Foundation/primitive tokens used directly in component styles.
- Side-effects (DOM manipulation, localStorage) in the dumb state store.

**Enforcement:**
- CI grep check: `rg "bg-white|text-gray-|bg-slate-" src/*/ui` MUST be empty.
- Code review: verify `ThemeController` location and state-store purity.

---

## 4. Ratification Checklist (PR Reviewers)

- [ ] All HTTP calls originate from the adapter/API layer.
- [ ] Domain layer contains only pure logic (no UI framework, state lib, browser APIs).
- [ ] Server state managed via data-fetching library; state store restricted to client-only sync state.
- [ ] All API responses validated by <%= _vl %> at boundary.
- [ ] Errors normalized to `AppError` and routed via notification bus.
- [ ] Loading-state semantics correct (first load vs. background refetch).
- [ ] Semantic tokens used exclusively in UI components.
